  "interpretation": "Most island-year colony rows share one census date, but 14 island-year cells are split across multiple dates, sometimes by weeks. Cross-island median dates are often close (median five-island span two days), with occasional large offsets. A simple model in which all same-island colonies are necessarily counted in one exact same-day batch is therefore false, but timing alone does not eliminate shared observer or protocol error.",
